c what would  your advice be to those people  i think if you want to give back don't  overthink it when i sat down with trevor  and when we were talking about these  issues we realize like this is not like  something that we need to overthink like  we can go attack this  you know it's very obvious that the work  you're doing has  a huge impact on the people that you're  helping but how has this work  changed you it's this idea of altruism  and paying it forward and that for me is  really really fulfilling i mean this is  like  a dream come true for me we had an event  we had a thanksgiving drive-through  where we fed  450 families in santa ana and we had a  lady who was  volunteering she came to me after and  she was crying and she was just  explaining you know how fulfilling that  day was for her  i think sometimes when we think about  volunteering and when we think about  giving back  we only think about the underprivileged  under-resourced  i think we we need to also think about  you know the people  like this lady it's this idea good for  you better for others right like  it feels good to donate local human  it's such a young organization it's  still in its infancy  yet you guys have done so much with it  where do you hope to go from here  the good thing about this is we don't  care about making money i'm in the nfl  i don't need a salary from this so my  only focus  is taking every dollar to impact people  so you know we're in a good position to  just  go crazy have fun and impact a lot of  people's lives  you're nominated for the walter payton  man of the year award for your  charitable work  off the field for being a positive  influence in your community  how does it feel to be recognized by the  nfl and by your team  for the work you're doing it's huge for  me and there's a mission to recognize  how blessed i am in my position and to  maximize that  as much as i can but it's just it's such  an honor you know  to to have my teammates and peers  recognize that